"""Carrhae: Mesopotamia, 53 BC.  A sample game for the Grognard engine.

Marcus Licinius Crassus, the richest man in Rome, has marched seven
legions into the open plain east of the Euphrates to win a war against
Parthia.  Surena, the Parthian general, meets him with ten thousand
horsemen and no infantry at all, and a train of camels loaded with
arrows.  Play either side against the computer, or against a friend at
the same screen.

Run it with ./carrhae (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.carrhae.json.  ./carrhae --selftest checks the map and plays
a game between two computer players.
"""

